1. Data Expectations

1.1. Data Completeness
- All ~400,000 active SCAN member records from the EDH source must be migrated to Microsoft Dataverse CRM with zero data loss.
- Each Member (Contact) record must have all mandatory demographic fields populated: First Name, Last Name, Member ID, Date of Birth, Main Phone, and Email.
- All related Enrollment (Care Plan), PCP History, Communication Preference, and Member Address records must be present and correctly linked to their parent Member.

1.2. Data Accuracy
- All migrated data must match the source EDH data with no discrepancies, as validated by reconciliation reports and random sample checks.
- All verification test scenarios (e.g., search by Member ID, Last Name + DOB) must return correct and matching records.

1.3. Data Format & Standards
- Phone numbers must conform to E.164 format (e.g., +1XXXXXXXXXX).
- Email addresses must comply with RFC 5322 standards (e.g., user@domain.com).
- All date fields must use ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD).
- Address fields must conform to USPS standards (Line1, City, State, Zip).

1.4. Data Consistency
- No duplicate Member ID records are allowed post-migration; deduplication must be completed prior to migration.
- All foreign key relationships (e.g., Member to Enrollment, PCP History, Communication Preference, Member Address) must be intact and valid.
- PHI fields must be consistently secured and accessible only by authorized roles.

2. Constraints

2.1. Mandatory Fields
- Member (Contact): First Name, Last Name, Member ID, Date of Birth, Main Phone, Email are mandatory.
- Enrollment, PCP History, Communication Preference, and Member Address must have valid references to the parent Member.

2.2. Uniqueness
- Member ID must be unique across all migrated records (max 15 characters).
- Source Record IDs must be unique within their respective entities.

2.3. Data Type & Format
- Phone: Text, E.164 format.
- Email: Text, RFC 5322 format.
- Date fields: Date/DateTime, ISO 8601 format.
- Boolean fields (e.g., Do Not Call, Is Preferred, Is Text Opt-In): 1 or 0.
- Address fields: Text, USPS standards.

2.4. Referential Integrity
- All child records (Enrollment, PCP History, Communication Preference, Member Address) must reference a valid Member (Contact) record.
- No orphaned child records are allowed.

2.5. Security & Access
- PHI fields must be secured per HIPAA; only authorized Advocate roles can access sensitive data.
- Role-based access controls must be enforced at the data model level.

2.6. Audit & Retention
- Migration audit logs must be retained for at least 18 months.
- Audit logs must capture record counts, success/failure status, and per-record error details.

2.7. Performance
- Post-migration search response time must be under 2 seconds for queries across all 400,000 records.
- Migration must complete within the agreed SLA batch window (e.g., 8 hours).

3. Business Rules

3.1. Migration & Data Processing
- Only active SCAN member records from EDH are in scope for migration.
- Pre-migration deduplication is mandatory; no duplicate Member IDs may exist in the target CRM.
- All field mappings must be implemented as specified; static values (e.g., Source System = 'EDH') must be set where required.
- All validation rules (phone, email, date, address) must be enforced during migration and in the target system.

3.2. Data Relationships & Linking
- Each Enrollment, PCP History, Communication Preference, and Member Address record must be linked to a valid Member (Contact) via foreign key.
- Deletion or update of a Member (Contact) must cascade or restrict changes to child entities as per referential integrity rules.

3.3. Security & Compliance
- PHI fields must be encrypted or otherwise protected in storage and transit.
- Only authorized Advocate roles may access PHI fields; unauthorized access attempts must be logged.
- Audit logs must be immutable and accessible for compliance review for at least 18 months.

3.4. Reporting & Validation
- All verification test scenarios (search by Member ID, Last Name + DOB, random sample validation, duplicate check, PHI access control) must pass prior to migration sign-off.
- Reconciliation reports must confirm zero data loss and no critical errors post-migration.
- All performance benchmarks (search response time, migration SLA) must be met before go-live.

